{
  "$type": "tech.scios.rrgi.evidence",
  "text": "CONTRADICTING: Live ApoE4 iCE-BECs were co-loaded with pH-sensitive Tf-pHrodo Red and pH-insensitive Tf-Alexa647. They showed a lower pHrodo/Alexa647 ratio per endosome than isogenic ApoE3 cells, which the authors read as HIGHER (less acidic) endosomal pH in ApoE4, the opposite of the reduced pH H1 predicts.",
  "description": "iPSC-derived brain endothelial cells (iCE-BECs) from two isogenic pairs. Pair 1: Bioni037-A (APOE3/E3, healthy donor fibroblasts) vs Bioni037-A4 (APOE4/E4, rs429358 edit). Pair 2: Alstem iPS26 (APOE3/E3) vs iPS16 (APOE4/E4, from bone marrow CD34+ cells). Cells were incubated 10 min with 25 µg/mL Tf-pHrodo Red plus 25 µg/mL Tf-Alexa647, then live-imaged at 100x. The intensity ratio was computed per colocalized endosome and analyzed by two-way ANOVA. Unit: n = 3 independent differentiations per isogenic pair, 30 cells per experiment. Caveat: brain endothelial cells, not astrocytes. The ratio is uncalibrated, so no absolute pH is reported. The authors note that this direction is opposite to the earlier astrocyte report.",
